Fixture review (2026-11-27)
  Every fixture under scripts/tests/ was read before shipping. No fixture holds
  a working exploit payload, shell code, credentials or a live target address,
  so no fixture was dropped or replaced.
  - sigma_match/events/*.json and events/correlation/*.json: log, proxy,
    file-event and process-creation samples. Addresses are 203.0.113.0/24
    (documentation range) and 10.0.0.0/8; hosts are *.example.test, web01,
    web02 and db02. The destructive command strings (rm -rf /var/www/html,
    rm -rf / --no-preserve-root, DROP TABLE customers, iptables -F) are
    telemetry values that pySigma matches in memory. No test executes them.
  - The guard audit marker in the fixtures is a detection signature and stays
    byte-identical.
  - scripts/artex_host_triage.py self-test: a synthetic ss line names the peer
    93.184.216.34 as the remote end of an established session, to prove that
    a non-listening socket is ignored. The script parses that text only and
    never connects to the address.
  - suricata/gen_pcap.py writes a file and sends no packet. The suite replays
    the bundled captures and does not run gen_pcap.py.
